# Insert before the existing LibreChat catch-all on the chosen HTTP or HTTPS origin.
# For an HTTP site, explicitly use an http:// site address in the enclosing Caddy block;
# for HTTPS, use the intended https:// address and valid certificate. Match actual port mapping.
# Choose the upstream transport for your deployment; a private/TLS connection or tunnel avoids
# transmitting SESSION cookies in plaintext between hosts. Caddy supplies X-Forwarded-Proto.
redir /metabase /metabase/ 308
handle_path /metabase/* {
    reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:3300 {
        header_down Location "^/(.*)$" "/metabase/$1"
    }
}
# Preserve CSP, X-Frame-Options and Set-Cookie. Never strip these headers.
# Metabase's Keycloak callback uses an absolute same-origin portal return URL,
# so the root-relative Metabase Location rewrite above cannot change /portal/data.
# Keep Keycloak and all existing subapplication routes and Compose overlays.
